# Database Schema Reference — PCB Placement Tracking System

**Database name:** `pcb_placement_db`
**Total tables:** 4 (`users`, `projects`, `component`, `placement_issues`)

This system tracks PCB (Printed Circuit Board) projects, the components placed on each board, and any placement issues found during inspection.

---

## 1. `users`

Stores the people who create/update projects and resolve issues. No CRUD API is exposed for this table — it exists purely as reference data, since full user management was outside the scope of this assignment.

| Column | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | INT (PK, AUTO_INCREMENT) | Unique user identifier |
| `name` | VARCHAR(100) | User's display name |
| `email` | VARCHAR(150), UNIQUE | User's email address |
| `role` | ENUM('admin','engineer','reviewer') | User's role in the system |
| `created_at` | DATETIME | When the user record was created |

---

## 2. `projects`

Represents a single PCB project/board design. Each project can have many components.

| Column | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | INT (PK, AUTO_INCREMENT) | Unique project identifier |
| `project_name` | VARCHAR(150) | Name of the project/board |
| `revision` | VARCHAR(100) | Revision label (e.g. "Rev B") |
| `updated_at` | DATETIME (auto) | Auto-updates on every change |
| `updated_by` | INT (FK → `users.id`) | User who last updated this project |
| `is_deleted` | TINYINT(1), default 0 | Soft-delete flag |

**Delete behavior:** Soft delete. Deleting a project marks it (and all its components) as `is_deleted = true`, rather than removing rows. This prevents accidental, irreversible loss of a project's entire component/issue history in one action.

**Relationship:** `projects.updated_by → users.id`

---

## 3. `component`

Represents one physical component placed on a project's board (e.g. a resistor, IC, connector). Each component belongs to exactly one project, and can have multiple placement issues logged against it.

| Column | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | INT (PK, AUTO_INCREMENT) | Unique component identifier |
| `project_id` | INT (FK → `projects.id`) | Project this component belongs to |
| `component_name` | VARCHAR(100) | Component's name/label (e.g. "U14 - Microcontroller") |
| `package` | VARCHAR(250) | Package type (e.g. "QFP-64") |
| `category` | ENUM('Passive','IC','Connector','Mechanical') | Component category |
| `placement_side` | VARCHAR(250) | Which side of the board (e.g. "Top") |
| `rotation` | DECIMAL(5,2) | Placement rotation in degrees |
| `x_position` | DECIMAL(6,3) | X coordinate (mm) |
| `y_position` | DECIMAL(6,3) | Y coordinate (mm) |
| `height` | DECIMAL(5,3) | Component height (mm) |
| `supplier` | VARCHAR(250) | Supplier/manufacturer name |
| `part_number` | VARCHAR(250) | Manufacturer part number |
| `status` | ENUM('verified','warning','critical','unverified') | Inspection status |
| `tolerance_position` | DECIMAL(5,3) | Allowed position tolerance (mm) |
| `tolerance_rotation` | DECIMAL(4,2) | Allowed rotation tolerance (degrees) |
| `image_url` | VARCHAR(250) | Reference image URL |
| `notes` | VARCHAR(255) | Free-text inspection notes |
| `created_at` | DATETIME (auto) | Set automatically on creation |
| `updated_at` | DATETIME (auto) | Auto-updates on every change |
| `is_deleted` | TINYINT(1), default 0 | Soft-delete flag |

**Delete behavior:** Soft delete, for the same reason as Projects — a component can have its own linked issues, so a soft delete avoids silently destroying that inspection history.

**Relationship:** `component.project_id → projects.id` (`ON DELETE CASCADE` at the database level, for cases outside the application's soft-delete path)

---

## 4. `placement_issues`

Represents a specific problem found on a component during inspection (e.g. a rotation mismatch, height violation). Each issue belongs to exactly one component.

| Column | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | INT (PK, AUTO_INCREMENT) | Unique issue identifier |
| `component_id` | INT (FK → `component.id`) | Component this issue was found on |
| `issue` | VARCHAR(255) | Description of the problem |
| `severity` | ENUM('warning','critical') | How serious the issue is |
| `status` | ENUM('open','in review','resolved') | Current resolution status |
| `created_at` | DATETIME (auto) | Set automatically on creation |

**Delete behavior:** Hard delete. Issues sit at the bottom of the data hierarchy — deleting one has no cascading effect on other tables, so there's no accidental-data-loss risk that would justify the extra complexity of soft delete here.

**Relationship:** `placement_issues.component_id → component.id` (`ON DELETE CASCADE`)

**Display note:** API responses for this table include a `reference` field — the linked component's name (e.g. "C236") — fetched via a JOIN with `component`, rather than stored directly, so it always stays in sync with the actual component data.

